<title>BRAZIL: Brazil IBGE sees smaller 1996 grains/oilseeds crop.</title>
<headline>Brazil IBGE sees smaller 1996 grains/oilseeds crop.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 grains and oilseeds harvest should total 72.92 million tonnes in 1996, down 8.13 percent from the 79.38 million produced in 1995, the National Statistics Institute (IBGE) said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>It did not however give a breakdown by crop.</p>
<p>The institute is planning to publish its forecast of planting intentions for the 1996/97 harvest in key regions in November.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
